>> B2: Describe how file descriptors are associated with open files.
>> Are file descriptors unique within the entire OS or just within a
>> single process?

File descriptors are managed per-process using struct f_desc in the thread's
fds list. Each descriptor maps an integer fd to an open struct file pointer.

File descriptors are unique only within a single process. Each process has its
own cur_fd counter starting at 2. Different processes can have the same fd
number representing different opened files.

